#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059469 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "733eab11-2a26-5402-8df5-bba50c9beaf9" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Cross Product Using Determinants"}] :question/id #uuid "d2698dbf-dea6-5abb-970e-a3ace180e337" :question/math-academy-id "e-4341" :question/problem "Let $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle 3,-4,1 \\rangle$ and $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle -7,0,2 \\rangle.$ Find $\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b}.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 3 & -4 & 1 \\\\ -7 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -7 & 2\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}3 & -4 \\\\ -7 & 0\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =((-4)\\cdot 2-1\\cdot 0)i-(3\\cdot 2-1\\cdot (-7))j+(3\\cdot 0-(-4)\\cdot (-7))k \\\\  & =-8i-13j-28k \\\\  & =⟨-8,-13,-28⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059470 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "21cef8c9-92ff-5527-a837-2236a0c1f9eb" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for an Unknown in an Equation Involving the Cross Product"}] :question/id #uuid "b834e666-de4f-5964-a280-6571ad44b6bd" :question/math-academy-id "e-4343" :question/problem "Let $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle 3, 1, 2x \\rangle,$ $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle 0,1,x \\rangle,$ and $|\\,\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b}\\,| = \\sqrt{19}.$ Find $x.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 3 & 1 & 2x \\\\ 0 & 1 & x\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2x \\\\ 1 & x\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}3 & 2x \\\\ 0 & x\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =-xi-3xj+3k \\\\  & =⟨-x,-3x,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{(-x)^{2}+(-3x)^{2}+{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{10{x}^{2}+9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & |\\,a\\times b\\,|=\\sqrt{19} \\\\  & \\sqrt{10{x}^{2}+9}=\\sqrt{19} \\\\  & 10{x}^{2}+9=19 \\\\  & 10{x}^{2}=10 \\\\  & {x}^{2}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x= \\pm 1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186303439 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "21cef8c9-92ff-5527-a837-2236a0c1f9eb" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for an Unknown in an Equation Involving the Cross Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "db20040e-bef4-51cd-947b-ee90d170929d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303441} {:answer/id #uuid "faedcfc3-3fa8-5c20-bf7a-c72cd7261dee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303442} {:answer/id #uuid "1b4ec3dd-346e-55d6-baa9-200d86a229b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-2,4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303443} {:answer/id #uuid "f55e0fa3-387c-5657-a2fc-ea0bceb8031f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303444} {:answer/id #uuid "6daa0145-bf33-529f-bb3b-02149dfe6f9f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-4,2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303445}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "db20040e-bef4-51cd-947b-ee90d170929d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303441} :answer-field/id #uuid "eab3d72b-5fd5-575e-b41f-09cd5ece7d50" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303440}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f571d284-38ad-50ae-b89e-87bf4db6e4ab" :question/math-academy-id "q-103540" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨2x,3,2⟩$, $b=⟨x,1,-1⟩$ and $|\\,a\\times b\\,|=\\sqrt{93}.$ Find $x.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2x & 3 & 2 \\\\ x & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}2x & 2 \\\\ x & -1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}2x & 3 \\\\ x & 1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(-3-2)i-(-2x-2x)j+(2x-3x)k \\\\  & =⟨-5,-4x,x⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{(-5)^{2}+(-4x)^{2}+{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25+16{x}^{2}+{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{17{x}^{2}+25}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{93} \\\\ \\sqrt{17{x}^{2}+25} & =\\sqrt{93} \\\\ 17{x}^{2}+25 & =93 \\\\ 17{x}^{2} & =68 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x=\\pm 2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186303446 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "21cef8c9-92ff-5527-a837-2236a0c1f9eb" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for an Unknown in an Equation Involving the Cross Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cca606c9-e50d-5425-957b-db71a8fabb2e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-3,9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303448} {:answer/id #uuid "67bd8ad0-1d67-5cfc-9ba2-2a3490c2a63a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{3},3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303449} {:answer/id #uuid "5b9b933a-4328-5b02-9c83-1bc0b01b08dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm 9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303450} {:answer/id #uuid "dbca431f-f8c5-5370-8367-5080f10591bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303451} {:answer/id #uuid "060ebcab-6b34-56bb-8d67-1f0732937168" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm \\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303452}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dbca431f-f8c5-5370-8367-5080f10591bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303451} :answer-field/id #uuid "3ffd1811-7344-5aa4-a404-ef0f34a29eb2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303447}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fa58a80f-ad5f-57b3-8136-8bf6f43c733c" :question/math-academy-id "q-103542" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨-1,2x,3⟩,$ $b=⟨2,-x,1⟩$ and $|\\,a\\times b\\,|=\\sqrt{355}.$ Find $x.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -1 & 2x & 3 \\\\ 2 & -x & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2x & 3 \\\\ -x & 1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2x \\\\ 2 & -x\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(2x+3x)i-(-1-6)j+(x-4x)k \\\\  & =⟨5x,7,-3x⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{(5x)^{2}+(7)^{2}+(-3x)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25{x}^{2}+49+9{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{34{x}^{2}+49}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{355} \\\\ \\sqrt{34{x}^{2}+49} & =\\sqrt{355} \\\\ 34{x}^{2}+49 & =355 \\\\ 34{x}^{2} & =306 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x=\\pm 3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304140 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "733eab11-2a26-5402-8df5-bba50c9beaf9" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Cross Product Using Determinants"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a4212f4-d006-5297-af36-1a524a7e0e1a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2j+3k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304142} {:answer/id #uuid "a7f86920-d48b-5bb1-929a-47d877dcb03e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "i-3j+6k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304143} {:answer/id #uuid "db451de7-5d82-5de4-acb8-dde80233194d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "i-2j+4k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304144} {:answer/id #uuid "0cef887d-ea75-5f48-ba74-3864a6efb0ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2j+4k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304145} {:answer/id #uuid "0e02933d-8cdf-58b3-af7a-0425474c7883" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3i+2j-4k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304146}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0cef887d-ea75-5f48-ba74-3864a6efb0ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2j+4k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304145} :answer-field/id #uuid "7428cc9d-be23-51c5-8628-2d9194a400da" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304141}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "032ca46b-c982-5019-abec-409ae74b9ee6" :question/math-academy-id "q-1396" :question/problem "Let $a=4i+2j-k$ and $b=2i+2j-k.$ Find $a\\times b.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 4 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(2\\cdot (-1)-(-1)\\cdot 2)i-(4\\cdot (-1)-(-1)\\cdot 2)j+(4\\cdot 2-2\\cdot 2)k \\\\  & =(-2+2)i-(-4+2)j+(8-4)k \\\\  & =2j+4k.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304147 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "733eab11-2a26-5402-8df5-bba50c9beaf9" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Cross Product Using Determinants"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "466b6d3e-0315-5f3d-8e50-6e46ccac1801" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7i+17j+31k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304149} {:answer/id #uuid "22264654-e6c7-5351-bb10-fec7409e5eea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25i+25j-25k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304150} {:answer/id #uuid "a1bc04e5-5ba5-5d6f-8d10-04942071fbc8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25i-17j-25k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304151} {:answer/id #uuid "3eb87888-d7bf-5553-bd51-561f95839738" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7i-17j+25k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304152} {:answer/id #uuid "fb752c85-4ae3-52cb-8fdf-18933ec2a268" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7i-17j-25k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304153}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fb752c85-4ae3-52cb-8fdf-18933ec2a268" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7i-17j-25k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304153} :answer-field/id #uuid "6826aeea-612e-578b-a4fc-b9a7bd65e2f7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304148}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1f7619fd-c9ea-5041-9ab8-7c9af799798b" :question/math-academy-id "q-1404" :question/problem "Let $u=7i+3j-4k$ and $v=-i-4j+3k.$ Find $u\\times v.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\times v & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 7 & 3 & -4 \\\\ -1 & -4 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 3\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}7 & -4 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}7 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -4\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(3\\cdot 3-(-4)\\cdot (-4))i-(7\\cdot 3-(-4)\\cdot (-1))j+(7\\cdot (-4)-(3)\\cdot (-1))k \\\\  & =(9-16)i-(21-4)j+(-28+3)k \\\\  & =-7i-17j-25k.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304154 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "733eab11-2a26-5402-8df5-bba50c9beaf9" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Cross Product Using Determinants"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "993a98d4-20cd-566d-9f82-3ffbeedf8a75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-29" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304156}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "993a98d4-20cd-566d-9f82-3ffbeedf8a75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-29" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304156} :answer-field/id #uuid "1795bf82-ea19-50ff-bc2a-07f8a600d105" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304155} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c7e6b2f5-b760-56bc-a31b-b8c0afa2c37f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304158}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c7e6b2f5-b760-56bc-a31b-b8c0afa2c37f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304158} :answer-field/id #uuid "b8b30046-a2be-5c15-a0c3-c09a040b3785" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304157} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "db66174d-aea5-5fa7-8a2b-273d64b55553" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304160}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "db66174d-aea5-5fa7-8a2b-273d64b55553" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304160} :answer-field/id #uuid "fc98d800-e65e-5497-a49b-af01b8892bc3" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304159}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e5b2e711-c105-5c4d-9045-58a44fcaf370" :question/math-academy-id "q-282143" :question/problem "Let $a=3i-4j+k$ and $b=-2i+5j+6k.$ Find $a\\times b.$\n\n$a\\times b=$\n\n{{field-1}}$\\,i\\,-\\,$\n{{field-2}}$\\,j\\,+\\,$\n{{field-3}}$\\,k$" :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 3 & -4 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 5 & 6\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-4 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 6\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 6\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}3 & -4 \\\\ -2 & 5\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =((-4)(6)-(1)(5))i-((3)(6)-(1)(-2))j+((3)(5)-(-4)(-2))k \\\\  & =(-24-5)i-(18+2)j+(15-8)k \\\\  & =-29\\,i-20\\,j+7\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304161 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "733eab11-2a26-5402-8df5-bba50c9beaf9" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Cross Product Using Determinants"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4358ec94-2445-526a-8c94-f45b074791a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "22" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304163} {:answer/id #uuid "0d562b62-ffb6-59bd-8f4c-a239a4e3feab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-22" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304164}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4358ec94-2445-526a-8c94-f45b074791a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "22" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304163} :answer-field/id #uuid "42d792d1-f57c-5045-8e86-c46394d2191b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304162} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7ed718d4-253f-5bae-8c6b-f09d4017b475" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304166}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7ed718d4-253f-5bae-8c6b-f09d4017b475" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304166} :answer-field/id #uuid "80f2f4cf-a6d8-5fcc-8682-9aff03774d0a" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304165} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7021764f-565a-5d91-81ec-1c49b83b60aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304168}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7021764f-565a-5d91-81ec-1c49b83b60aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304168} :answer-field/id #uuid "dca99414-c830-5428-bd59-4968a1ffc441" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304167}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d3d339cf-a2da-5b23-8253-57bcf9590e44" :question/math-academy-id "q-282144" :question/problem "Let $a=i+2j-5k$ and $b=-3i+4j+k.$ Find $a\\times b.$\n\n$a\\times b=$\n\n{{field-1}}$\\,i\\,+\\,$\n{{field-2}}$\\,j\\,+\\,$\n{{field-3}}$\\,k$" :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 2 & -5 \\\\ -3 & 4 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & -5 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(2\\cdot 1-(-5)(4))i-(1\\cdot 1-(-5)(-3))j+(1\\cdot 4-2\\cdot (-3))k \\\\  & =(2+20)i-(1-15)j+(4+6)k \\\\  & =22\\,i+14\\,j+10\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304169 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "733eab11-2a26-5402-8df5-bba50c9beaf9" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Cross Product Using Determinants"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2f1cd693-fca6-54e3-974c-371441de532f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304171}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2f1cd693-fca6-54e3-974c-371441de532f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304171} :answer-field/id #uuid "8dff6861-99c2-56b4-94af-885cf23fcb7d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304170} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "68bd3100-7410-5a36-825a-6fee38785970" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304173}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "68bd3100-7410-5a36-825a-6fee38785970" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304173} :answer-field/id #uuid "1fd7069e-5621-5dd1-a4f7-e1d72aaf77ab" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304172} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3048a8a7-1ac5-5f7a-a8bf-68fd4868f7ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304175}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3048a8a7-1ac5-5f7a-a8bf-68fd4868f7ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304175} :answer-field/id #uuid "035c933d-742f-5388-803f-c7a7c2cb71b5" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304174}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "559fdfc9-944f-5db4-9235-36c1fd68b65f" :question/math-academy-id "q-282147" :question/problem "Let $a=-4i+3k$ and $b=i+2j-2k.$ Find $a\\times b.$\n\n$a\\times b=$\n\n{{field-1}}$\\,i\\,-\\,$\n{{field-2}}$\\,j\\,-\\,$\n{{field-3}}$\\,k$" :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -4 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-4 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-4 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(0)(-2)-(3)(2)i-(-4)(-2)-(3)(1)j+(-4)(2)-(0)(1)k \\\\  & =(0-6)i-(8-3)j+(-8-0)k \\\\  & =-6\\,i-5\\,j-8\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304176 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "21cef8c9-92ff-5527-a837-2236a0c1f9eb" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for an Unknown in an Equation Involving the Cross Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4eb9364a-9cb1-566b-8666-0684d16efb9a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304178}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4eb9364a-9cb1-566b-8666-0684d16efb9a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304178} :answer-field/id #uuid "20e34428-29f0-542f-9d60-9a0a2f1e0f43" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304177}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b0420859-e854-5686-a566-28a8ac19b277" :question/math-academy-id "q-282270" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨x,1,2⟩,$ $b=⟨1,0,2⟩$ and $|\\,a\\times b\\,|=\\sqrt{5}.$ Find $x.$\n\n$\\,x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ x & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}x & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}x & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(2-0)i-(2x-2)j+(0-1)k \\\\  & =⟨2,2-2x,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(2-2x)^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+(4{x}^{2}-8x+4)+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{x}^{2}-8x+9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{5} \\\\ \\sqrt{4{x}^{2}-8x+9} & =\\sqrt{5} \\\\ 4{x}^{2}-8x+9 & =5 \\\\ 4{x}^{2}-8x+4 & =0 \\\\ (2x-2)^{2} & =0 \\\\ 2x-2 & =0 \\\\ x & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304179 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "21cef8c9-92ff-5527-a837-2236a0c1f9eb" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for an Unknown in an Equation Involving the Cross Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7dcb1cbd-94dd-5ec7-a370-51627c867ef2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304181}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7dcb1cbd-94dd-5ec7-a370-51627c867ef2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304181} :answer-field/id #uuid "bcb4ef77-6cb3-5d3f-b4c1-653cc0729217" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304180} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4dee8668-d5bd-5bbb-8e15-abc9e8c4f1ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304183}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4dee8668-d5bd-5bbb-8e15-abc9e8c4f1ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304183} :answer-field/id #uuid "0b2f2c49-3c37-5b34-953e-85c4bdac5471" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304182}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "077d8348-aacc-5cfe-9c4f-83cd2cce459b" :question/math-academy-id "q-282278" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨2x,1,4⟩,$ $b=⟨3,0,2⟩$ and $|\\,a\\times b\\,|=\\sqrt{157}.$ Then, in **ascending order**, the possible values of $x$ are\n\n$\\,x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ and $\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2x & 1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}2x & 4 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}2x & 1 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(2-0)i-(4x-12)j+(0-3)k \\\\  & =⟨2,12-4x,-3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(12-4x)^{2}+(-3)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+(144-96x+16{x}^{2})+9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16{x}^{2}-96x+157}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{157} \\\\ \\sqrt{16{x}^{2}-96x+157} & =\\sqrt{157} \\\\ 16{x}^{2}-96x+157 & =157 \\\\ 16{x}^{2}-96x & =0 \\\\ 16x(x-6) & =0 \\\\ x & =0,\\,x=6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the solutions are $x=0,$ $x=6.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304184 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "21cef8c9-92ff-5527-a837-2236a0c1f9eb" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for an Unknown in an Equation Involving the Cross Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "75b4e25f-1030-5b07-89ea-2c0a3d618edc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304186} {:answer/id #uuid "67d14441-a0c9-5061-a93c-e5acee68411f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304187} {:answer/id #uuid "69682917-4196-5bce-8932-d2047ba4f27f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304188} {:answer/id #uuid "2cb2ab75-866a-5bcb-b308-7f16325a231f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm \\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304189} {:answer/id #uuid "e51be6ff-88ca-52a1-b0ad-255306fa8a2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm \\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304190}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2cb2ab75-866a-5bcb-b308-7f16325a231f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm \\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304189} :answer-field/id #uuid "87a9aae2-c040-564a-9d2d-e42640d1113c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304185}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "54ac0cd9-756f-56ec-a02b-bc51faafb7b6" :question/math-academy-id "q-77427" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨2,x,1⟩,$ $b=⟨1,-x,3⟩$ and $|\\,a\\times b\\,|=10.$ Find $x.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & x & 1 \\\\ 1 & -x & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}x & 1 \\\\ -x & 3\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}2 & x \\\\ 1 & -x\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(3x+x)i-(6-1)j+(-2x-x)k \\\\  & =⟨4x,-5,-3x⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{(4x)^{2}+(-5)^{2}+(-3x)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16{x}^{2}+25+9{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25({x}^{2}+1)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =10 \\\\ \\sqrt{25({x}^{2}+1)} & =10 \\\\ 25({x}^{2}+1) & =100 \\\\ {x}^{2}+1 & =4 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x=\\pm \\sqrt{3}.$"}]}
